    {
      "id": "be-s12m-perfect-competition-c2",
      "heading": "Setting price and output",
      "explanation_md": "The **market\\** sets the price where supply meets demand. The single firm sees a **flat demand line\\** at that price: it can sell as much as it likes at Pe, and nothing above it.\n\nEvery firm maximizes profit where **MR = MC\\**. For a price taker MR is the price, so the rule becomes **P = MC\\**.\n\nOn the graph, follow the price line across until it hits the **MC\\** curve. Drop down: that is the best output **Qf\\***. The **profit\\** is the box between the price and **ATC\\** at that output: **(Pe - ATC) x Qf\\***.",
      "example_ids": [],
      "key_terms": [],
      "exam_line": "Price taker: set P = MC. Profit = (Pe - ATC) x Qf*.",
      "clarification": null,
